00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:06.090
Loops are extremely powerful for repeating the same set of commands

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.540
over and over, but with different values.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.190
A for loop starts with the word for, and an equation

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.480
that defines the loop variable, the thing that

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.690
is going to change its initial value each time you go through the loop.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.480
In this case, the loop variable is iX.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.790
The values that the loop variable will take in this case are 1, 3, and 2.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.000
The loop variable will take on a different value

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.840
each time you go through the loop.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.100
In this case, there are three values in the array,

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.157
so we will execute the loop three times.

00:00:34.157 --> 00:00:35.990
The first time, we will go through the loop,

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:38.980
iX will have the value 1 because it&amp;#39;s the first value

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.107
in the array in the loop declaration.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.440
The first time we go through the loop, the for statement

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.980
is equivalent to typing iX equals 1.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.930
The loop now executes every command until it gets the word &amp;quot;end.&amp;quot;

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:53.210
In this case, the only command is to say the value of the number.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.140
One.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.119
The code now returns to the for loop declaration.

00:00:57.119 --> 00:00:59.160
Now, we are going through the loop a second time.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.720
In this case, iX will be 3 because 3 is a second value in the array inner loop

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.010
declaration.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.440
Now, the loop does its thing.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.960
This process continues for each value in the loop declaration array.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.340
Then we&amp;#39;re done with the loop.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.960
MATLAB continues with the code after the end statement.

